{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest tour, by Held–Karp dynamic programming (Bellman, “Dynamic programming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"treatment of the travelling salesman problem”, Journal of the ACM 9, 1962; Held and Karp,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“A dynamic programming approach to sequencing problems”, Journal of SIAM 10, 1962): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none; among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeldKarpTSP"},{"type":"text","text":"’s tour). The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three vertices."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"shortestTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentif